Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 15:59:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Support for fetching configs for isolated processes

This will replace a previous approach of checking if execmem is denied.
Previously, the check is done upon initialization of isolated services,
as prior to Android 17, isolated service always use Android Runtime,
which determines if Javascript should always run in JITless mode, along
with WebAssembly.

This new approach binds an isolated service early on the main process
initialization for browser, and the embedding app for webview, as a
single source of truth whether execmem is denied for isolated process.
This now also provides a way for the main process to check if execmem is
blocked to disable toggles as needed.
